--- draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-22-1
STATEMENT: An endorsement of a promissory note must be valid to be effective.
QUOTE: (1) The endorsement of the promissory was not valid. The assignment of the promissory note did not constitute payment as P's wife did not accept it as payment. There was failure of consideration even if the note was accepted as consideration. (2) If a transferee has obtained property in good faith and for valuable consideration the property cannot in any case be followed into his hands and no decree for specific performance can be obtained against him. Nor can any one seeking specific performance against such purchaser invoke the assistance of s. 93 of the Trusts Ordinance. Section 93 of the Trusts Ordinance imposes
STATUTE: 
